    "notes": "Inspected all 11 current portable views. The mapped outer compound, cruciform raised platform, taller central sanctuary, staggered face-tower cluster, open colonnades and interrupted gallery roofs distinguish Bayon. Two separately mapped eastern libraries remain separate forms within the gallery compound. Near levels use actual four-sided facial relief: broad noses, cheeks, downcast eyelids, shallow smiling lips and elongated ears; these are faceted visualization geometry, not photo decals. The first draft had an oversized square central head and too many complete gallery roofs; the central lower core, head proportions and broken roof rhythm were revised against the ordinary pictures."
