    "notes": "Reviewed approximate full-site placement on the unchanged 161-square/6m standard DEM. Raw east/south coordinates preserve the nearly cardinal gallery grid and eastern approach. The opaque cruciform platform supports the principal cluster. Gallery supports, outer tower feet and library foundations extend below sampled terrain; district gallery supports include extra depth for their longer grouped bays. No terrain or water excavation is requested. Full-site loading replaces 12 temple records and preserves all 52 independent buildings in the 960m tile exactly. Eight native water features retain 438179.1610115951 square metres. Failure retains all 64 native buildings; eviction preserves surfaces and frees model geometry. A synthetic 64m partial tile retains original terrain beneath clipped pieces. Its empty semantic context checks clipping/lifecycle only; temporary cut faces are not permanent temple geometry. Coarse canopy-influenced DEM levels are not archaeological survey elevations."
  },
  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Accepted for the specific medium-fi Bayon exterior and approximate normal-map/DEM placement. Twelve standard-map records control the outer compound, inner cruciform platform, eight principal tower parts and two eastern libraries. The 37 rendered tower forms include 29 secondary position/height estimates from ordinary pictures and a modern explanatory layout whose caption explicitly says upper-terrace dimensions are approximate. This is not a surveyed current tower, face or damage inventory. The nominal 43m central top, subsidiary heights, crown tiers, face proportions, roof survivors, stairs and archaeological thresholds remain visualization estimates. Exact carvings, inscriptions, lichen patterns, navigable interiors, surrounding monuments and historic complete roofs are outside scope. Coarse canopy-influenced terrain does not resolve the actual archaeological paving levels. No bespoke survey or archival research was used."
  },
